[2.323583,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2J\r\n  Follow OSPF from Hello to a usable route\r\n  ========================================\r\n\r\n  Ze and FRR share frr0 on 172.29.0.0/24. FRR advertises loopback\r\n  10.255.1.2/32. Ze initially has no OSPF configuration.\r\n\r\n  We explain these sections as they are loaded and committed:\r\n\r\n    1. Give the router an area\r\n    2. Match the shared-link timers\r\n    3. Introduce a Hello mismatch\r\n    4. Restore the matching Hello interval\r\n\r\n  The last two are deliberate live changes after the initial proof.\r\n"]
